    "description": {
      "value": "<p><strong>Ironbedside Manner.</strong> You have learned to be calm, precise, and a little terrifying when things are bad.</p><ul><li>You gain a small mechanical bonus on <strong>Faith (Soul) checks</strong> to stabilize, treat injuries, or assess physical trauma.</li><li>When you attempt to <strong>stabilize a dying creature</strong>, a roll of 9 or lower on the 2d10x10 counts as a 10 for that attempt (once per creature per Soma Break).</li></ul>",
